Yeah. You just like shove all that stuff in there that one day every four years.

00:02:29.440 --> 00:02:38.240
Right. The game starts pretty normally with, it was a robot producing exploration planet like any other.

00:02:39.460 --> 00:02:42.740
Okay, that's definitely like, that is tongue in cheek, right?

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:44.400
Like it knows, right?

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:47.140
Like they know that that was, that's ridiculous.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.260
I think so. I love that.

00:02:49.480 --> 00:02:51.300
I love the boldness of that statement.

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:55.960
Yeah. And of course it wasn't a robot producing exploration planet like any other.

00:02:56.120 --> 00:02:58.620
There are problems and you're going to have to solve them.

00:02:59.440 --> 00:03:05.900
But we don't really get like, I guess in the manual there is more about like your mission and everything and the explanation.

00:03:06.140 --> 00:03:08.680
But we don't really know the Low-G-Man.

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:10.860
We don't know why he's the Low-G-Man.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:16.300
Yeah, does he have, I mean, is it just because this, this planet has low gravity, right?

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:21.360
It's not like he has some special attribute that makes him like not affected by gravity, right?

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:24.820
I think he has like, no, you're right.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:28.260
You're right. Sorry. Everybody has like anti-gravity technology.

00:03:28.260 --> 00:03:29.940
I don't think it's this planet.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:31.360
Oh. That has.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:32.980
I see. According to the manual.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:34.760
There's tech. Yeah, there's tech.

00:03:34.960 --> 00:03:39.080
So everybody technically, he doesn't have like, he didn't make it from the ground up.

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:40.460
Like he has these special boots.

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:41.460
Would be great.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:43.000
I feel like that's a better story.

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:53.360
But most of the enemies in the game also like either, you know, just like are flying or, you know, act as if they have low gravity themselves.

00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:57.740
So I understand why you might think that it's the planet and not the people.

00:03:57.940 --> 00:04:01.760
But because also like these are, these are not like jumps.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:08.120
These are moon jumps, you know, these are like epic long, you're hang time in the air for a while.

00:04:08.120 --> 00:04:09.700
And it grows to it.

00:04:09.800 --> 00:04:14.740
It grows to like three screens worth of normal height.

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:27.680
You can travel, you know, in one singular level like that high and just kind of hang out there and hop over like a variety of enemies and just skip those areas completely.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:33.000
They really are embracing the low gravityness of it.

00:04:33.080 --> 00:04:37.180
It's not just like, oh, yeah, he jumps a little bit higher or like he has a jet pack.

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:39.920
No, he can jump really high.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:45.720
Yeah. And there is something oddly satisfying about having like a high jump.

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:50.480
It reminds me of when I was a kid playing like 007 games.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:59.220
I'm thinking specifically Nightfire, but it definitely like came into play in earlier games as well, where you can turn the you could turn the gravity all the way down.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:04.440
And there's something just like really fun about just flying around the stages and shooting at each other.

00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:09.400
And yeah, this this captures that same kind of feeling because it's like there's like a.

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:15.560
There's an action excitement to it that you don't get just from a regular jump.

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:28.000
This also has just while we're talking about the controls of low G man, this has a feature that I feel like became like a lot more prominent later on other consoles.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:37.980
But there's moving, which, you know, feels a little bit like a walk, but a power walk, not slower by any means of just obviously using the left and right D pad.

00:05:38.260 --> 00:05:43.800
But then if you tap it twice and then hold down low G man runs.

00:05:43.800 --> 00:05:45.980
And that's like that's pretty cool.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:55.320
Like, I feel like that's something you see more in like the 3D error before that, you know, before it became like, oh, just hold down a different button to run at all times.

00:05:55.320 --> 00:05:58.100
I like this double tap to get a little more speed.

00:05:58.360 --> 00:05:59.620
OK, I'm going to be honest.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:01.100
You just blew my mind.

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:03.100
I had no idea this was an option.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:07.580
Did you find it was helpful to have that extra speed?

00:06:07.740 --> 00:06:11.020
Because now. No, I actually just thought it was like innovative for the console.

00:06:11.460 --> 00:06:14.340
Yes, because I had no idea that this is this was the case.

00:06:14.460 --> 00:06:22.260
But as I'm thinking back on these levels, I can't think of a time where I really wanted to run much faster because there's always an enemy or something right there.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:24.540
I feel like this is a little more.

00:06:25.020 --> 00:06:30.260
You got to be a little more cerebral about your movement than running really fast would allow.

00:06:30.260 --> 00:06:32.380
But that's me speaking about it having not tried it.

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:40.680
So I don't know. No, yeah, it's especially weird because as you're alluding to, like you want to be in the air a lot of this game.

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:43.080
And so you you're not running at all when you're in the air.

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:46.200
It's not it's not like it boosts you further by any means.

00:06:46.720 --> 00:07:00.920
So it's a little strange to to to not think about the like to think about the game as if it's a platformer where it's really just kind of like you're a vertical, not a height game necessarily.

00:07:00.920 --> 00:07:11.480
Like you're not you're not you're really not climbing up that much, but you are using the height to your advantage to to get around things and to get over enemies and to, you know, choose your battles.

00:07:11.480 --> 00:07:18.400
I think a large part of this game relies on skipping over content.

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:19.200
Mm hmm.

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:21.540
And also, like, I think that the jump.

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:25.240
Oddly, well, it like, yeah, allows you to skip over things.

00:07:25.460 --> 00:07:37.600
It does add a a different type of like gameplay that you don't normally think of, of like the precision of where you land is very important because I mean, we haven't gotten into it yet.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:46.140
But the only way to really like the most consistent way to really attack enemies is by like landing on them with this.

00:07:46.400 --> 00:07:47.600
I don't know. Was it a spear?

00:07:47.940 --> 00:07:48.760
Yeah, it's a spear.

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.480
You're landing on them or hitting them from below and firing up.

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:57.000
You cannot fire this spear horizontally in any way.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:08:05.200
So a lot of your attacks rely on you jumping to like avoid an enemy and then landing on them while hitting the spear button.

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:12.000
And it's surprisingly a little more difficult than you think to land where you want to land with with enough precision to hit these things.

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:15.860
So it it's different than any game that we've played in that sense.

00:08:16.060 --> 00:08:20.260
Yeah, especially because, yeah, the low gravity of it all makes it very floaty.

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:25.740
And and the platforms or the enemies rather are a little small when you consider how much you're floating.

00:08:26.600 --> 00:08:32.840
Joe, as you mentioned, that is the only way to really attack enemies outside of getting some special power ups.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:45.300
So the main way that you fight as the low gravity man is with what I thought was a freeze gun, but is actually a electromagnetic disruptor pistol in EMDP.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:49.160
We can remember that acronym for a while.

00:08:50.060 --> 00:08:52.520
Electromagnetic. I mean, electromagnetic.

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:54.060
Isn't that like one word?

00:08:54.440 --> 00:08:56.680
Yeah, it's a dash.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:57.720
It's got a dash in it.

00:08:57.920 --> 00:08:59.660
OK, I don't know if that's true.

00:08:59.660 --> 00:09:02.020
It just says that in this manual it has a dash.

00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:05.420
So EMDP and you use that.

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:08.500
And I thought that was like an actual pistol.

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:15.180
Like you you shoot this at an enemy and it would take them out, but it freezes them in place, but not forever either.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:17.220
It just kind of freezes them momentarily.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:19.200
So you've got to, you know, handle them.

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:24.200
And so I was like, OK, what's my like, how do I switch guns?

00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.360
How do I get out of the freeze gun and go to the pistol?

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:29.120
And there is no like pistol.

00:09:29.240 --> 00:09:30.080
And I was like reading about it.

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:33.160
I was like, OK, there's some power ups that I don't have yet.

00:09:33.160 --> 00:09:35.600
And I was seeing on the pause screen.

00:09:36.160 --> 00:09:39.060
How do I get those power ups so I can finally start defeating enemies?

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:45.700
And then I looked in the manual and found out the incredibly like complicated.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:57.820
But because of the system they've laid out, the only way to really handle this is you have to be like the direction in the D pad that you want the spear to go.

00:09:57.940 --> 00:09:59.720
But only up and down, not left and right.

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:01.340
Up or down.

00:10:01.340 --> 00:10:08.020
And then the A button or sorry, and then the B button in order to use your spear.

00:10:08.380 --> 00:10:11.700
So if it sounds complicated, it is.

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:18.020
But imagine like in Zelda 2 Adventure of Link, Link has that down smash with the sword.

00:10:18.160 --> 00:10:28.340
If instead to do that with the spear, you had to jump first, hold down on the D pad and the attack button in order to launch your spear out.

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:40.660
And so what you do is you wind up freezing enemies, jumping on top of them and then just pressing down on the D pad and your attack button in order to just kind of continuously stab them with your spear while they're frozen.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:42.320
It's a very vicious experience.

00:10:42.460 --> 00:10:43.520
It sure is. Yeah.

00:10:43.840 --> 00:10:47.660
But I guess I didn't think about how I appreciated this until right now.

00:10:47.760 --> 00:10:52.340
But I do appreciate that when you freeze an enemy, they don't hurt you when you touch them.

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:54.520
Because I feel like a lot of other games would do it that way.

00:10:54.960 --> 00:10:57.840
It's nice that you can stand on them and then press down.

00:10:57.840 --> 00:10:59.940
Didn't we just have that with Little Nemo?

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:07.440
I was just going to say, what is going on with these projectiles that just freeze the enemies in two games?

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:10.060
And I guess they both kind of did it for a similar reason.

00:11:10.060 --> 00:11:15.920
I'm assuming that the reason it's like that in this is to make you feel like you need to use the jump more.

00:11:16.060 --> 00:11:20.500
But I guess it really, maybe this one doesn't pull it off quite as much.

00:11:20.600 --> 00:11:24.940
Because it's like, just because you froze an enemy doesn't mean you need to jump really high all the time, you know?

00:11:25.940 --> 00:11:28.500
Did you have that learning moment, though, with the spear?

00:11:28.780 --> 00:11:32.520
Because I didn't know about the spear when I started.

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:35.640
And I just legitimately couldn't find a way to attack.

00:11:35.640 --> 00:11:36.540
I was stuck.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:38.260
I had that also.

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:40.820
I think I was testing to see, can I shoot up?

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:42.100
Because this thing was above me.

00:11:42.180 --> 00:11:43.380
I was trying to shoot my gun up.

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:45.200
And then the spear came out.

00:11:45.260 --> 00:11:49.180
I was like, oh, okay. And then, you know, naturally I tried doing it downwards.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:51.260
And I did try for a while.

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:52.840
I was like, there's got to be a way to do this horizontally.

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:54.960
But it seems that there isn't.

00:11:55.360 --> 00:12:05.200
Since the game really relies on the low gravity aspect, though, is that a positive or a negative based on the way they've designed the game?

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:09.640
Like, does it feel more like a chore to use the low gravity?

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:11.620
Or does it feel too easy?

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:16.880
Or is it just like, this is the interesting, this is the most interesting part of this game?

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:24.180
I, all right, I think that so far, everything I've said, after I say it, I'm like, wow, that sounded really positive.

00:12:24.580 --> 00:12:29.760
But I actually have, like, a lot more negative opinions on this game than I've let on so far.

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:37.320
And one of them is that, while I think the idea of this, like, game designed around a high jump, and, like, I think that that's cool.

00:12:37.480 --> 00:12:41.000
I don't think they really designed this game very well around the high jump.

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:43.600
Like, that's their idea.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:57.560
But I'm not, I don't, I don't feel there are too many situations where I wouldn't just be more comfortable just fighting, like, treating this like a regular game and shooting at something.

00:12:57.560 --> 00:13:03.800
Or, like, half the time when I want to jump on something, I don't want to jump that high, because it's right in front of me, and I just want to jump up and land on it.

00:13:03.980 --> 00:13:15.320
So, like, it's cool, but I do think that they just, like, missed a huge opportunity to, like, really design their game around it in ways that made me, like, want to use it all the time.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:28.000
Yeah, and even in the levels where there is some verticality to them, or even just some of the boss fights, there's that one after, it's the second stage, and, you know, you have to be, like, inside.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:31.460
You have to go through the boss, he's like a robot, and then get on top of his head.

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:41.300
Like, again, it becomes more challenging because of the jump, whereas if you were, like, Mega Man, right, you would have more precise movement.

00:13:41.480 --> 00:13:45.300
I guess that's the point, but it doesn't mean that it's enjoyable.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:53.220
And then on the other side of that, even though this isn't directly tied to the actual, like, gameplay design of the controls,

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:58.780
the animation in general for this game is, like, a little choppy.

00:13:59.180 --> 00:14:06.000
Yeah, it feels oddly like games I remember from earlier in the podcast.

00:14:06.260 --> 00:14:13.980
And, you know, this is, I think I allude to this a lot, and I liked this game, but it reminds me of Rygar,

00:14:14.740 --> 00:14:19.200
which I like, I liked Rygar a lot, I voted it essential at the time.

00:14:19.760 --> 00:14:29.300
But I think I've seen enough NES games that, beyond that, and I'm talking specifically about, like, the animation graphic little style,

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:33.440
not the gameplay and everything, but, like, it feels dated a little bit at this point.

00:14:34.200 --> 00:14:45.540
Yeah. And beyond, like, just the character animations, and by choppy, I mean, like, it literally feels like they're not drawing all the frames of animation or something.

00:14:45.540 --> 00:14:50.560
Like, and I get it, they probably, the game's probably running at 60 FPS like all other NES games.

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:55.920
It's just that they didn't draw enough of the movement, so they just kind of hang on certain sprites,

00:14:56.080 --> 00:15:01.520
and they just look like the sprites are, like, statically moving horizontally across a screen.

00:15:01.820 --> 00:15:11.800
But speaking of horizontal, there's, like, a, there's a weird pause or stutter in the horizontal movement of this game,

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:15.240
which is funny because, like, the vertical doesn't have the same problem.

00:15:15.460 --> 00:15:20.360
But the way things kind of, like, not load in, it doesn't have, like, that Super Mario Bros.

00:15:20.460 --> 00:15:22.660
3 thing where, like, you see it on both sides.

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:31.560
It's just, for whatever reason, it's not smooth left to right, but it is up to down.

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:32.880
Like, I don't know why that is.

00:15:32.980 --> 00:15:34.640
Like, I can't imagine why that's the case.

00:15:34.640 --> 00:15:43.220
Yeah, I mean, I wonder if they just, I mean, I wonder if it was intentional to make it feel like, oh, you're this, like, big guy moving clunkily forward,

00:15:43.240 --> 00:15:46.740
but, you know, you got low gravity, so you jump up and it's this very smooth arc.

00:15:47.060 --> 00:15:57.240
Yeah, so the low gravity is actually only upwards, and moving left to right is actually very high gravity,

00:15:57.240 --> 00:15:58.640
so there's some friction there, right?

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:00.660
Yeah, yeah. It feels like you're walking in the wind or something.

00:16:00.660 --> 00:16:09.460
Right. There's the gravity, in order to make it low gravity upwards, they had to turn some of the gravity 90 degrees,

00:16:09.460 --> 00:16:11.200
so it's actually pushing back at you.

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:21.020
While you do have other power-up weapons, I would say that, like, the most interesting addition of this game for weapons or movement at all

00:16:21.020 --> 00:16:30.020
is that certain enemies or robots that you destroy, you then gain access to their, like, vehicle, if you will.

00:16:30.120 --> 00:16:39.320
So you have, like, walking robots that you can, like, jump in, and now you have, like, a bigger shot,

00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:45.580
and then you have, like, flying vehicles that you can get into, and then you have, like, this spider vehicle that you can get into,

00:16:45.580 --> 00:16:52.640
and they're all just, like, they're all just different kinds of flavor and definitely make low G-Man feel stronger,

00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:59.860
but I thought that was kind of a neat touch that, like, the ones that even the enemies are controlling you can then hop into.

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:02.500
It felt very Halo in that regard.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:11.980
Yeah, so I'm not a big Halo guy, but I gotta admit that, like, I appreciate this level, like, this addition to that kind of thing.

00:17:12.100 --> 00:17:20.320
I just, I wonder if adding something like this, if the resources to put this in could have been better spent somewhere else.

00:17:20.440 --> 00:17:23.140
Like, how necessary did you find this?

00:17:23.460 --> 00:17:25.040
No, yeah, agreed.

00:17:25.240 --> 00:17:27.980
They're just different flavors of getting through the level.

00:17:28.140 --> 00:17:30.660
They're not, like, roadblocks that you need.

00:17:30.660 --> 00:17:37.680
Like, make sure you have that spider vehicle so that you can climb on these walls and get over this area.

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:40.020
It's just like, hey, and now here's a different way.

00:17:40.460 --> 00:17:44.600
And it kind of, like, removes the low gravity element a little bit.

00:17:44.800 --> 00:17:51.560
Like, they still move, and some of them are even fly, but it's, like, it's much more controlled than low G-Man's jump,

00:17:51.560 --> 00:17:56.780
so it's kind of, like, trivializing the one aspect that they were designing the game around,

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:58.920
or at least theoretically were designing the game around.

00:17:58.920 --> 00:18:05.780
Yeah, I mean, I like the idea of it, but it's just, I guess I just, maybe I'm being too negative now.

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:14.480
I'm overcompensating for my positivity earlier, but I just wish that they became a master of something

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:16.580
before they tried to become, like, a jack of everything.

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:20.420
Not that, like, they try to do everything in this game, but I just still,

00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:24.600
it still hasn't sold me on the main gimmick of this game yet, you know?

00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:30.520
Yeah, so, going into that, and you don't have to have an answer prepared, I'm just asking you this on the fly,

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:35.580
but, like, if you were to make a low gravity man game, right,

00:18:35.720 --> 00:18:40.020
I already can imagine just the level design alone on how I would handle it,

00:18:40.060 --> 00:18:43.640
because, again, these are very, for the most part, closed, like, at one point,

00:18:43.820 --> 00:18:45.400
like, the entire level takes place in a cave.

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:47.800
It's like, why would no G-Man fight in a cave?

00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:51.600
Like, why would he go into a space that limits his movement?

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:56.780
But, nevertheless, like, what would you do, Joe, if you're starting over?

00:18:57.020 --> 00:19:02.320
Well, so, off the top of my head, I think what I would want is, well, one, to be, yeah, more open,

00:19:02.480 --> 00:19:08.180
fewer caves, but then also, they do have some vertical levels,

00:19:08.180 --> 00:19:12.520
but make a lot more verticality in the game, and make it, like, you know,

00:19:12.600 --> 00:19:15.720
it should really feel, not just like, oh, I can jump really high,

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:18.600
so I can get above these enemies and then come down on them,

00:19:18.620 --> 00:19:22.780
but also, like, being able to jump really high should be what gives me advantages.

00:19:22.780 --> 00:19:26.100
Give me more power-ups to make me jump higher to let me reach places.

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:29.960
Put some, like, I don't know, put springs, maybe not literal springs,

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:33.180
but, like, something like that that launches you even further, or, like,

00:19:33.600 --> 00:19:38.080
I kind of try, like, I'm thinking of, like, what Sonic the Hedgehog was trying to do with speed,

00:19:38.080 --> 00:19:40.400
but for, like, jumping, you know?

00:19:40.720 --> 00:19:42.920
Add a bunch of things that, like, enhance it.

00:19:42.920 --> 00:19:45.980
Yeah, you bring up a great point, because as you said that about, like,

00:19:46.100 --> 00:19:49.240
making the levels more vertical, you made me think, it's true,

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:54.740
Super Mario Bros. 2 is a more vertical platformer than this game ever was.

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:58.720
Right. And, like, even, like, boss battles, like, make your boss battles,

00:19:58.860 --> 00:20:02.420
put their weak spots way up on top of their head, like, skyscraper level.

00:20:02.540 --> 00:20:04.580
You gotta jump up their, you know, maybe not skyscraper level,

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:10.640
but, like, make it so it seems like you have a reason for jumping really high.

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:14.360
Low G-Man should have at least one Shadow of the Colossus-style fight,

00:20:14.380 --> 00:20:18.260
where he has to scale up an enemy in order to get to their head.

00:20:18.840 --> 00:20:25.200
Yes, and it should be in the same fidelity as the remastered Shadow of the Colossus.

00:20:25.540 --> 00:20:27.160
Right, right, just that one scene, though.

00:20:27.160 --> 00:20:28.060
Just that level, yeah.

00:20:28.220 --> 00:20:34.740
Yeah, yeah. Okay, well, so, since we were talking about the game with, you know, fondness,

00:20:34.740 --> 00:20:39.880
I will start to talk about some, again, they're mostly, like, buggy complaints about the game,

00:20:40.020 --> 00:20:41.280
but things I just didn't like.

00:20:41.560 --> 00:20:45.620
And one of them, for sure, was the way that after you kill an enemy,

00:20:45.820 --> 00:20:47.980
how you receive its power-ups.

00:20:48.500 --> 00:20:50.020
This is nonsense.

00:20:50.180 --> 00:20:51.760
This has never been done in a game before.

00:20:51.880 --> 00:20:53.180
This doesn't need to be done here.

00:20:53.620 --> 00:20:55.120
I say never been done in a game before.

00:20:55.120 --> 00:20:56.880
I realize it's probably done in every shmup,

00:20:56.940 --> 00:20:59.820
but at least in those, like, they don't fall, like, that way.

00:20:59.820 --> 00:21:06.640
So the way it works is you defeat an enemy, and the power-up, like, spawns out of them,

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:12.440
and then immediately, as if it has no gravity at all, or as if it's very heavy gravity,

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:18.160
it gets pulled into the Earth's core, a.k.a.

00:21:18.180 --> 00:21:19.260
the bottom of the screen,

00:21:19.520 --> 00:21:23.560
and disappears immediately if you weren't directly standing over the enemy.

00:21:23.560 --> 00:21:31.880
It is very hard to catch any of that stuff if you didn't know that the enemy was about to spawn said power-up.

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:33.560
So you wind up losing a lot of those.

00:21:33.880 --> 00:21:35.960
Why couldn't it just drop into the ground?

00:21:36.300 --> 00:21:39.180
Right. It doesn't interact with the floor in any way.

00:21:39.380 --> 00:21:40.440
And, like, I'm trying to remember.

00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:42.320
I feel like some of them are not even just power-ups.

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:43.700
Some of them are, like, physical things.

00:21:43.760 --> 00:21:46.820
Are there not? Or are they all, like, little energy-looking power-ups?

00:21:47.380 --> 00:21:48.440
Uh, that's a good question.

00:21:48.440 --> 00:21:49.600
Because there's not, like, a gun or something, is there?

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:51.000
I don't think you get a gun.

00:21:51.560 --> 00:21:54.660
What are these, all, like, made out of lightsaber?

00:21:54.940 --> 00:21:59.280
Where they all just, like, immediately just burn through the whole ground

00:21:59.280 --> 00:22:01.060
and sink to the bottom of the Earth?

00:22:01.820 --> 00:22:05.880
Yeah, so you collect a boomerang, a fireball, a wave.

00:22:06.640 --> 00:22:07.440
A boomerang.

00:22:07.740 --> 00:22:08.840
It is a boomerang.

00:22:08.920 --> 00:22:10.000
It's a physical boomerang.

00:22:10.100 --> 00:22:12.180
It's not, like, boomerang essence energy.

00:22:12.180 --> 00:22:13.340
It's just a boomerang.

00:22:13.500 --> 00:22:15.500
Yeah, yeah, exactly. But why does it not hit the ground?

00:22:16.000 --> 00:22:17.040
I can't understand.

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:19.320
It is the icon of a boomerang, though.

00:22:19.320 --> 00:22:21.820
Like, it still has the square block around it.

00:22:21.880 --> 00:22:24.980
Sure. So maybe it's just, you know, beyond our comprehension.

00:22:25.300 --> 00:22:28.940
I mean, I'm being a little silly here, but it's just funny to me.

00:22:30.200 --> 00:22:35.100
Joe, just for the record, because we always watch these long plays.

00:22:35.880 --> 00:22:37.200
LoG, man, I didn't get up to it.

00:22:37.280 --> 00:22:41.300
But Chapter 3-2B, which is just a crazy way to talk about a level,

00:22:41.440 --> 00:22:43.460
as if, like, as if these are crazy long.

00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:46.140
This is 22 minutes into a 42-minute long play.

00:22:46.280 --> 00:22:52.880
But Chapter 3-2B, that boss does have what you were looking for,

00:22:53.100 --> 00:22:54.460
an enemy that does...

00:22:55.300 --> 00:22:58.360
Yeah, it's like kind of the, like, buggy thing up on the mountain, sort of,

00:22:58.460 --> 00:22:59.740
or above the mountain. Exactly, yes. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:22:59.840 --> 00:23:03.780
And you do have to, like, carefully land on top of it in order to strike it

00:23:03.780 --> 00:23:08.100
and everything. But the reason I brought that in is because I do have a good segue for it.

00:23:08.100 --> 00:23:12.960
The boss fights in general are also a confusing, buggy thing,

00:23:12.960 --> 00:23:15.940
at least the first time you encounter one.

00:23:16.400 --> 00:23:20.620
I don't know about you, but when I ran into my first boss on the very first stage,

00:23:20.760 --> 00:23:21.840
I didn't know it was a boss.

00:23:21.940 --> 00:23:23.340
I just thought it was just another enemy.

00:23:23.720 --> 00:23:25.660
I didn't realize that was at the end of the level,

00:23:25.680 --> 00:23:27.460
because it just fell down into something.

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:30.720
And when I froze it and then started attacking it,

00:23:30.880 --> 00:23:35.520
I thought it wasn't working because there is no feedback if it's frozen.

00:23:35.520 --> 00:23:38.760
Yeah, and is that consistent for all the bosses?

00:23:38.860 --> 00:23:41.520
I feel like some gave me feedback and others didn't.

00:23:41.660 --> 00:23:45.380
Every boss will give you feedback if they're not frozen.

00:23:45.580 --> 00:23:50.560
Right, okay. However, enemies do give you feedback if they're frozen,

00:23:50.560 --> 00:23:53.840
so why are the bosses the exception to the rule?

00:23:54.180 --> 00:23:55.960
Yeah, I didn't even realize that.

00:23:56.080 --> 00:23:58.260
Like, I think I had that frustration without even, like,

00:23:58.320 --> 00:24:00.420
consciously realizing what it was.

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:03.560
But, yeah, and the bosses, yeah, like,

00:24:03.560 --> 00:24:05.460
you would fall into a pit or something,

00:24:05.580 --> 00:24:07.360
and it just looks like another regular enemy.

00:24:07.700 --> 00:24:09.540
Some bosses, it's like you're at the end of the stage,

00:24:09.560 --> 00:24:10.620
and it's this big, giant thing.

00:24:10.820 --> 00:24:13.060
And other bosses look like little enemies.

00:24:13.200 --> 00:24:16.040
And I imagine there's some difference I didn't pick up on.

00:24:16.100 --> 00:24:20.060
Like, oh, these are just, like, the mid-world bosses or mid-stage bosses,

00:24:20.140 --> 00:24:21.940
and the other ones are, like, the end, you know,

00:24:21.940 --> 00:24:26.160
once you're in, like, 2B instead of 2A bosses or whatever.

00:24:26.160 --> 00:24:31.340
But it was just not always clear when I was fighting a boss and when I wasn't.

00:24:31.760 --> 00:24:34.700
And because some of these, you fall into a pit to fight,

00:24:34.840 --> 00:24:38.400
and they're, like, moving back and forth even when you can't see them,

00:24:38.480 --> 00:24:42.220
a lot of times you fall, you just better hope you don't land on them

00:24:42.220 --> 00:24:43.480
because you can't see where they are.

00:24:43.840 --> 00:24:47.140
And sometimes that would be, like, a level ender for me,

00:24:47.180 --> 00:24:48.480
where it's just like, yeah, I jumped into the pit,

00:24:48.520 --> 00:24:49.900
I landed immediately on the boss.

00:24:50.660 --> 00:24:52.740
I have to rescind my comment, though, Joe.

00:24:53.020 --> 00:24:57.360
It's just a, you know, I'm learning, I'm misremembering it.

00:24:57.820 --> 00:24:58.980
It's true of all enemies.

00:24:59.160 --> 00:25:01.300
They don't have feedback when you freeze them.

00:25:01.580 --> 00:25:04.680
However, most enemies don't require as many hits.

00:25:04.780 --> 00:25:07.480
Yeah, they just die. So it's like you're getting the instant feedback,

00:25:08.220 --> 00:25:11.620
which you don't get, obviously, with the boss fights.

00:25:33.200 --> 00:25:35.340
You joked on the beginning of the episode

00:25:35.340 --> 00:25:37.980
that the sequel would be called Dead Man's Chest,

00:25:38.180 --> 00:25:41.040
but there is no Low G-Man sequel, Joe.

00:25:41.220 --> 00:25:43.020
Does that disappoint you? No.

00:25:44.920 --> 00:25:47.100
I don't know where they would go from here.

00:25:47.820 --> 00:25:49.180
Yeah, I mean...

00:25:49.580 --> 00:25:51.680
Low H-Man? I guess if this...

00:25:51.680 --> 00:25:53.500
Well, if this was successful,

00:25:53.600 --> 00:25:55.360
I have no idea what the success of this was,

00:25:55.480 --> 00:25:56.800
but if it had been successful,

00:25:57.560 --> 00:26:02.240
I could see them just trying to hone it,

00:26:02.860 --> 00:26:04.240
polish it, and make, like, a...

00:26:04.240 --> 00:26:06.900
Like, I feel like it could have been, like,

