oh, Low G-Man 2, everybody knows that game,

00:26:09.980 --> 00:26:11.220
and, like, was there a Low G-Man 1?

00:26:11.900 --> 00:26:13.040
You know, like, I feel like it would have been, like,

00:26:13.080 --> 00:26:15.440
that situation, because I think that there's potential.

00:26:15.780 --> 00:26:17.280
You know, like, a sequel...

00:26:17.280 --> 00:26:20.980
I wouldn't even necessarily, like, shy away from, like,

00:26:21.220 --> 00:26:22.220
there being a sequel.

00:26:22.460 --> 00:26:29.520
I would welcome it, because I'd want to see how they could expand on this concept.

00:26:30.220 --> 00:26:31.240
Yeah, I...

00:26:31.240 --> 00:26:34.480
We usually don't cover, like, every game's endings,

00:26:34.540 --> 00:26:37.700
but I don't know definitively if this had, like,

00:26:38.340 --> 00:26:41.640
a cliffhanger or anything to it,

00:26:41.700 --> 00:26:43.360
but, like, yeah, sometimes, you know,

00:26:43.460 --> 00:26:47.880
like, you play a game and you just naturally expect that there would be a sequel,

00:26:47.980 --> 00:26:49.580
especially for these old NES games.

00:26:49.760 --> 00:26:52.140
Like, somebody surely eventually said, like,

00:26:52.160 --> 00:26:53.720
you know what franchise we should resurrect?

